# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Writer's Kiosk configuration template
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env` (in the same folder as the executable
#    or the folder you run `dotnet run` from).
# 2. Fill in the values for ONE provider below.
# 3. NEVER commit the real .env file. The .gitignore in this project
#    already excludes it.
#
# NOTE: a line starting with "#" is a comment and is IGNORED. The
# optional settings below are shown commented out; to turn one on,
# remove the leading "# " so the line starts with the setting name
# (e.g. change "# PRINT_DUPLEX=long" to "PRINT_DUPLEX=long").
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which API to use: "openai" or "azure"
LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# ── Option A: OpenAI ──────────────────────────────────────────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_ME
# Any vision-capable model works; gpt-4o is the default.
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# ── Option B: Azure OpenAI (school/district tenants often use this)
# Two sign-in styles:
#  1) KEYLESS (recommended): leave AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY unset. The first
#     launch opens a browser sign-in with your district account; tokens
#     are cached encrypted (Windows DPAPI) so later launches are silent.
#     Your account needs the "Cognitive Services OpenAI User" role on
#     the Azure OpenAI resource. No API key ever exists on disk.
#  2) API KEY: set AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY and it is used instead.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE-NAME.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-06-01
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=          (leave unset for keyless sign-in)
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=               (optional: pin your district's tenant)
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=               (optional: IT-registered app id, if the
#                                 tenant requires an approved app)
# AZURE_AUTH=entra               (optional explicit override: entra|key)

# ── Hardware (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Which camera to use if more than one is plugged in (0 = first).
# A saved teacher profile (Profiles menu) overrides this at launch.
CAMERA_INDEX=0

# Windows only: full path to SumatraPDF.exe for fully silent printing.
# If unset, the app looks in the usual install locations, and falls
# back to the default Windows PDF print handler if not found.
# SUMATRA_PATH=C:\Program Files\SumatraPDF\SumatraPDF.exe

# Print to a specific printer instead of the system default (optional).
# PRINTER_NAME=Library Laser 2

# Double-sided printing, if the printer supports duplex (e.g. Lexmark
# MS310d): "long" flips on the long edge like a book (recommended);
# "short" flips on the short edge. Needs SumatraPDF; unset = single-sided.
# PRINT_DUPLEX=long

# File with the teacher's notes about today's assignment (optional; read
# at startup and used to focus the feedback). Default: assignment.txt in
# the folder the kiosk runs from — see assignment.example.txt.
# ASSIGNMENT_FILE=assignment.txt

# Start with the camera image flipped, for upside-down or mirrored
# camera mounts. Applies to the preview AND the image sent for feedback.
# Also togglable live with the V (vertical) / H (horizontal) keys.
# FLIP_VERTICAL=1
# FLIP_HORIZONTAL=0

# Software auto white balance + exposure correction for dark or
# color-tinted cameras (default on; the E key toggles it live).
# ENHANCE=1

# Seconds to wait after one submission finishes before the next can
# start (guards against spacebar-mashing running up API costs).
# Default 8; set 0 to disable.
# COOLDOWN_SECONDS=8

# Teacher review log: each report's text (never images, never names) is
# appended to feedback-log\YYYY-MM-DD.md so the teacher can review the
# AI's feedback after class and reprint after a printer jam.
# Default on; set 0 to disable.
# FEEDBACK_LOG=1

# ── Safety notices (mandated-reporting support) ───────────────────
# If a submission appears to contain a real personal disclosure (abuse,
# self-harm, threat of harm), nothing prints; the student sees a calm
# "Please bring this page to your teacher," and the event is written to
# the in-app Activity Log and feedback-log\safety-log.md (metadata only —
# never content or identity; the kiosk knows neither).
# Optionally, the district can also be notified: set this to a
# district-managed notification flow URL (e.g. Power Automate "When an
# HTTP request is received") and the kiosk POSTs minimal JSON (station,
# time) there; the FLOW then emails the school's teacher-of-record,
# counselor, and principal lists, which IT maintains centrally.
# ENABLING THIS IS AN ADMINISTRATIVE DECISION — coordinate with your
# school before setting it. An alert is an internal notification, never
# the legal report; the educator remains the mandated reporter.
# SAFETY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://prod-00.eastus2.logic.azure.com/workflows/...
# STATION_NAME=Room 214 kiosk        (identifies the station in alerts;
#                                     defaults to the computer's name)

# Pin the kiosk window to a screen position, e.g. an extended display.
# Coordinates are virtual-desktop pixels: with a 1920-wide main monitor,
# a second monitor to its right starts at WINDOW_X=1920, WINDOW_Y=0.
# WINDOW_X=1920
# WINDOW_Y=0
